.TH HA_PUSH 8 "2026-05-09" "thermoservice 0.7" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ha_push \- push DS18B20 temperature reading to Home Assistant REST API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ha_push.py
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ha_push.py
reads the current temperature from the local DS18B20 1-Wire sensor and pushes
the reading to a Home Assistant instance via its REST API (States endpoint).
.PP
The script is normally invoked by the
.B thermoservice-homeassistant.timer
systemd timer every 60 seconds.  It creates or updates the entity
.B sensor.thermoservice_temperature
in Home Assistant with attributes including unit of measurement, device class,
friendly name, sensor ROM, and hostname.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HASS_URL
Base URL of the Home Assistant instance (default:
.IR http://localhost:8123 ).
.TP
.B HASS_TOKEN
Long-lived access token used for Bearer authentication.  Generate one in Home
Assistant under
.B Profile \(->  Security \(-> Long-Lived Access Tokens .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/thermoservice/ha_push.py
Script installed by the
.B thermoservice-homeassistant
package.
.TP
.I /etc/default/thermoservice-homeassistant
Drop-in configuration file; set
.B HASS_URL
and
.B HASS_TOKEN
here.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/thermoservice-homeassistant.service
oneshot service unit that runs
.BR ha_push.py .
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/thermoservice-homeassistant.timer
Timer unit that triggers the service every 60 seconds.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Reading was pushed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
No sensor found, or HTTP request to Home Assistant failed.
.SH EXAMPLE
Configure credentials and enable the timer:
.PP
.RS
.EX
echo 'HASS_URL=http://homeassistant.local:8123' | sudo tee /etc/default/thermoservice-homeassistant
echo 'HASS_TOKEN=<token>' | sudo tee -a /etc/default/thermoservice-homeassistant
sudo systemctl enable --now thermoservice-homeassistant.timer
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thermo (1),
.BR thermoservice (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
